<title>BELGIUM: BANK DEGROOF RATES BEKAERT.</title>
<headline>BANK DEGROOF RATES BEKAERT.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Summary of research report -</p>
<p>Co name-----------Sector------Price------Broker-------------</p>
<p>    Bekaert	 Steel cord/wire 21,000*    Bank Degroof</p>
<p>COMMENT: Investors have overreacted to recent profit warning</p>
<p>and competition from DuPont's Kevlar for use in car tyres.</p>
<p>Bekaert's 1996 profits to be hit by downturn in steel cord</p>
<p>prices in last quarter 1996. But medium-term profit growth</p>
<p>potential impressive due to recovery in dlr, stg. Restructuring</p>
<p>of steel cord division should contribute 1.5 billion francs a</p>
<p>year to operating profit once complete. Group earnings should</p>
<p>double by 2000 to around 2,200 francs a share.</p>
<p>Recommendation: BUY. Analyst: Peter De Neve</p>
<p>(*) Date of research report: 27/02/97</p>
<p> Estimates:   EPS	  pvs est   P/E     Gross dividend</p>
<p> 1995	   1,399 BFR    n/a     15.0    600 BFR</p>
<p> 1996	     816 BFR    n/a     25.7    600 BFR</p>
<p> 1997	   1,117 BFR    n/a     18.8    667 BFR</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
